[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Campfires"
brief_tooltip = "Fires need fuel to stay lit.
Nearby units receive a warmth bonus.
Fire goes out when fuel runs out."
implemented = true
detailed_text = "[b]Fire & Fuel[/b]

[i]In the Arctic, fire is life. The expedition carried coal and spirit fuel, but supplies dwindled quickly. Men burned anything they could find — ship timbers, spare clothing, even books — to keep the cold at bay for one more night.[/i]

A lit campfire provides warmth to all units nearby. Without fuel, it goes out.

[b]How Fires Work[/b]

• Right-click a campfire to open its fuel panel
• Add fuel from a nearby unit's inventory — wood, coal, or other combustibles
• Each fuel type burns for a different length of time
• When the fuel runs out, the fire dies

[b]Warmth[/b]

Any unit standing near a burning fire receives a warmth bonus each hour. Combined with shelter, a fire can keep your men alive through the worst blizzards.

[b]Tips[/b]

• Keep a fire burning through the night — temperatures drop sharply after dark
• Stockpile firewood at the workbench before winter arrives
• Place fires near shelters so men benefit from both warmth sources
• A fire without fuel is useless — check fuel levels regularly"
